WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.735
 Gentlemen, congratulations.

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:04.670
You are both moving forward
into the third and final round

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.005
of this competition.

00:00:06.071 --> 00:00:07.240
Now, in this last
round we're going

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:08.941
to ask you to go back
to your home forges

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:10.843
and build an iconic
weapon from history that

00:00:10.909 --> 00:00:12.411
has been shrouded in mystery.

00:00:12.478 --> 00:00:14.781
Gentlemen, we want
you to build this--

00:00:20.185 --> 00:00:22.655
the Medieval Sword of Mystery.

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:27.994
The Medieval Sword of Mystery
has been puzzling historians

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.462
for centuries.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.630
This double-edged broadsword
features a double fuller,

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:34.700
making it light enough to
wield single-handed, delivering

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:36.269
fast, lethal strikes.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:40.640
The sword was found in the River
Witham in East England in 1825.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.175
It's believed to
have been forged

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:45.445
back in the 13th century,
although its exact origin

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.446
is a mystery.

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:48.114
Even more mysterious,
the blade has

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:51.117
a gold inlaid inscription
etched into the steel

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.585
in an unknown language.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:55.354
Several years ago, the
British Museum recruited

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.123
the public to help decipher it.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:01.160
But to this day, no one has
been able to crack the code.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.494
Bladesmiths, you
will have four days

00:01:02.561 --> 00:01:04.731
to build your medieval
swords of mystery.

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:05.698
So, good luck.

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:06.699
See you guys in four days.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:07.567
 Good luck.

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:08.334
 Good luck, buddy.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:14.207 line:8%
LARRY: My name is Larry
Rhodes, 44 years old.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.875 line:14%
I live in Fulton, Kansas.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.677
I'm kind of a perfectionist,
kind of from the old school.

00:01:18.777 --> 00:01:22.014
If you're going to do it, do
it right or don't do it at all.

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:24.383
I think what I need
to do to win is

00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:26.185
I need to hit the wow factor.

00:01:26.251 --> 00:01:28.187
That's ready to go in the forge.

00:01:28.253 --> 00:01:30.823
I'm going to run two
billets at the same time

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:31.991
so I'm not waiting on it.

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:36.362
All right, here we
go, billet number two.

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:39.298
Got good welds on it, and
I'm thinking it will be OK.

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.067
I'm going to grab
the two billets,

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.569
put a right-hand twist in
one, and a left-hand twist

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:46.572
in the other, cut them
up and restack them.

00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:47.574
Well, here we go.

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:53.579
Well, it looks like I have
a piece with a crack in it.

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:57.750
It starts here, goes
down, over, and back up.

00:01:57.816 --> 00:02:01.220
I'm going to go ahead and go
to plan B. I got a bar of 5160,

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.122
so I'm just going to go
ahead and put it in the forge

00:02:03.222 --> 00:02:05.458
and run it on out.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.126
Looking forward
for the wow factor.

00:02:07.226 --> 00:02:08.227
It's not going to happen.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.796
All right, here we go.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:16.969
Perfect.

00:02:17.035 --> 00:02:19.171
Right now we're back on track.

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:20.906
Yeah, it's a good
and straight blade.

00:02:21.006 --> 00:02:22.307
I'm going to concentrate
on the handle.

00:02:22.374 --> 00:02:24.343
It' starting to look
like a guard [inaudible]..

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.812
First up, I think I'm
going to weld a bolt on it

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:28.447
for a threaded pommel.

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:31.017
Well, that looks very
good, but too bad.

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.351
I put my handle together.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:33.919
I want to make sure
to get a tight fit.

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:35.288
Don't want anything loose.

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:36.156
Ooh!

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:41.227
I wished I had more
time on the detail work,

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:44.229
but let's go in there and
test it and let's get her done

00:02:44.296 --> 00:02:44.997
and get it over with.

00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:45.832
I'm ready.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.204 line:8%
CORDALE: My name is
Cordale Whitfield.

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:55.408 line:8%
I'm 20 years old, and I'm
from Telephone, Texas.

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:59.378
I love bladesmithing because
I just like fire and metal.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:01.714
Now for the spicy bit.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.884
As I'm going to quench, I
really hope I don't pull it

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.320 line:14%
out and turn it into a banana.

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:15.594
Now is the grind marathon.

00:03:15.661 --> 00:03:18.531
Today I definitely have
to finish the handle.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.065
I know exactly what
I'm going to do.

00:03:20.165 --> 00:03:21.267
I'm going to do a leather stack.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.401
With a leather stack,
and I got to do

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.136
is stack it up,
glue it together,

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:25.672
and put the pommel on.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.073
So, onto leather.

00:03:27.139 --> 00:03:30.009
I just got to finish shaping
the handle, I got to sharpen it,

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:31.643
and then that's it.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:34.012
For this part of the
program, we will now start

00:03:34.079 --> 00:03:35.848
at the mystery inscription.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:39.017
A medieval mystery sword
got a mysterious inscription

00:03:39.084 --> 00:03:40.719
that nobody can figure out.

00:03:40.819 --> 00:03:42.755
Pretty good.

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:46.525
I'm going to scratch off the
letters, and I'll etch that,

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:48.294
and then I'll just
etch the letters

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:49.762
and it will leave
my blade shiny.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.364
I believe that's gonna work.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:52.731
I like how it turned out.

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:53.733
Oh, yeah.

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:54.901
That's a pretty sharp blade.

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:57.937
Let's go chop up
some water bottles.

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:01.507
There you go.

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:02.909
He gone.

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:05.111
I'm definitely
proud of this sword.

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:07.246
I can't wait to see it
tested, and hopefully

00:04:07.346 --> 00:04:08.814
come away with that 10 grand.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:12.418
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:15.354
The legendary Medieval
Sword of Mystery.

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:17.323
Well, the first mystery we're
going to solve right now

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.291
is are they lethal?

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:20.326
Cordale, you're up first.

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:21.293
You ready for this?

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.261
 I suppose.

00:04:22.361 --> 00:04:24.930
 All right, let's do this.

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:28.268
[music playing]

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:48.921
All right, Cordale, let's
talk about your Medieval Sword

00:04:49.021 --> 00:04:50.389
of Mystery.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.424
First up, your
handle construction.

00:04:52.524 --> 00:04:54.827
Your handle is nice and smooth.

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:58.264
The one issue I have is
it has all this space.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:00.866
Now, let's talk about your edge.

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.601
These boars are no joke.

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:04.804
They're very tough
to cut through,

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:10.509
but your edge made easy cuts
and thrust on this boar carcass.

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:14.980
And I finally figured out what
that word right there says--

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:16.682
"it will kill."

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:17.649
 Thank you.

00:05:17.749 --> 00:05:18.951
 Larry, your turn, sir.
Are you ready?

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:19.719
 Yes, sir.

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:20.520
 Let's do this.

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:34.233
Guys, I think we have
a parameter issue here

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:35.901
that we need to talk about.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:36.736
 Quick huddle?

00:05:52.184 --> 00:05:54.587
Well, Larry, it seems that Doug
saw something with your blade

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:56.288
that he wants to discuss
further with the judges.

00:05:56.388 --> 00:05:57.723
So gentlemen, while
they talk, I'm

00:05:57.823 --> 00:05:59.592
going to ask you to please
step off the forge floor.

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:03.996
All right, the guys are out.

00:06:04.062 --> 00:06:05.564
What did you see?

00:06:05.664 --> 00:06:10.403
 Well, what I did not see on
Larry's sword is a disk pommel.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:14.140
We asked him to replicate
an iconic legendary Medieval

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:15.741
Sword of Mystery.

00:06:15.807 --> 00:06:18.444
That's not a style of a blade,
that's one particular blade.

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:21.380
When you look at that, it's
got one form, one look.

00:06:21.446 --> 00:06:23.148
 We put these parameters
down, because we

00:06:23.248 --> 00:06:25.084
want everything to test evenly.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.253
It's not the sword we asked for.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:29.522
 Yeah, this pommel
is not a vague idea.

00:06:29.589 --> 00:06:33.592
You wanted this pommel for
counterbalance on the blade.

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:37.162
Also, you want that swell where
it is much larger than the

00:06:37.262 --> 00:06:39.198
handle itself for retention.

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:42.368
But what we have on Larry's,
it actually tapers smaller

00:06:42.434 --> 00:06:44.337
than the handle, so
there's a good chance

00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:46.405
of swinging it and having
it fly out of your hand

00:06:46.505 --> 00:06:48.274
and endanger people around you.

00:06:48.374 --> 00:06:49.942
 Well, you guys all
on the same page?

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:51.144
 Yeah.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:51.944
 All right, we'll
call them back in.

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:58.184
All right, Larry, we
got a bit of an issue.

00:06:58.284 --> 00:07:01.620
We asked you guys to recreate
the Medieval Sword of Mystery.

00:07:01.687 --> 00:07:05.357
Now, part of that sword
is the disk-shaped pommel.

00:07:05.424 --> 00:07:06.659
The judges have
talked it through,

00:07:06.725 --> 00:07:08.460
and they've decided that
your pommel does not

00:07:08.561 --> 00:07:11.530
fit within the definition
of a disk-shaped pommel,

00:07:11.596 --> 00:07:14.933
so unfortunately, it
is a parameter failure.

00:07:15.033 --> 00:07:17.570
 Larry, one of the parameters
for the Sword of Mystery

00:07:17.636 --> 00:07:19.004
was a disk pommel.

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:21.339
Two biggest reasons for
that, aside from the fact

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.042
it was part of the
original design,

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:26.612
is having that mass back
there to retain the sword

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:29.348
while it's being
swung, also, the weight

00:07:29.448 --> 00:07:31.383
to counterbalance the blade.

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.452
Your pommel doesn't
have that, and we're

00:07:33.518 --> 00:07:35.220
worried that swinging
that, it could

00:07:35.287 --> 00:07:37.423
go flying across the room.

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:39.057
 Well, Larry, you
fought hard through this,

00:07:39.157 --> 00:07:41.827
but unfortunately, with the
parameter failure and the fact

00:07:41.927 --> 00:07:44.597
that the judges can't test your
blade fairly against Cordale's,

00:07:44.664 --> 00:07:45.932
I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:07:46.032 --> 00:07:47.467
step off the forge floor.

00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:49.067
 Thank you for [inaudible]
gentleman, appreciate it.

00:07:49.167 --> 00:07:50.269
- Thank you.
- Good fight.

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:51.503
LARRY: Yeah, I'm
disappointed with it.

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:53.672
I wanted to see it perform.

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:55.808
I was running up against
the clock, running close,

00:07:55.875 --> 00:07:58.677
so I worked up to the last
minute getting it done,

00:07:58.744 --> 00:07:59.945
and I forgot my disk pommel.

00:08:00.045 --> 00:08:04.783
That's how it goes,
but I had a good time.

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:06.818
 Well, Cordale, your
hard work paid off.

00:08:06.885 --> 00:08:08.821
You are the newest
Forged in Fire champion,

00:08:08.921 --> 00:08:11.791
and you just won yourself
a check for $10,000.

00:08:11.858 --> 00:08:12.390
Congratulations.

00:08:12.457 --> 00:08:14.060
 Thank you.

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:15.294
I'm pretty excited.

00:08:15.361 --> 00:08:16.661
I hate to win it
this way, but I'm

00:08:16.761 --> 00:08:19.098
excited to win it nonetheless.

00:08:19.198 --> 00:08:20.765
 You won, fair and square.

00:08:20.832 --> 00:08:22.000
Well done.
- Good job, Cordale.

00:08:22.067 --> 00:08:23.169
Good job.

00:08:23.269 --> 00:08:24.703
 I doubt I'll
make another sword,

00:08:24.803 --> 00:08:28.774
but I was very happy with my
blade and I had a lot of fun.

